      "side": 1,
      "message": "While studying the segmentation feature in the encoder we have noticed a syntax signaling issue related to `mode_ref_delta_enabled` flag. As per AV1 specification, Section 5.9.11 (Loop filter params syntax), syntaxes related to loop filter delta should be nested under `mode_ref_delta_enabled` condition (Please refer decodeframe.c: line 1780-1792). However, the encoder writes a `meaningful` update bit to the bitstream regardless of whether `mode_ref_delta_enabled` was true or false. This issue was originally introduced in [CL98781](https://aomedia-review.googlesource.com/c/aom/+/98781).\n \nSince this flag is hardcoded as enabled, the issue was not seen by default. The issue can be reproduced by modifying the code (i.e., by setting `mode_ref_delta_enabled \u003d 1` to `mode_ref_delta_enabled \u003d 0` in the code). This CL resolves the issue by nesting the delta update signaling under the `mode_ref_delta_enabled` check. The fix is bit-exact for all default encodes.\n \nTo add a unit test, we would need to introduce a test-only codec control API in the encoder interface (similar to `AV1E_ENABLE_MOTION_VECTOR_UNIT_TEST`). Please let us know your opinion on adding an API and unit test to the codebase.",
      "revId": "b537ca7c588adf02888a986bd1f27f7433140aa4",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
